`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The repo's convention for broker-dependent clients (`io.nats:jnats`, MQTT via `eclipse-mosquitto`) is to spin up a Docker container by hand in `@BeforeAll` via `ProcessBuilder`, pinned to the exact tag in `tests/tck-build-logic/.../allowed-docker-images/`, rather than using Testcontainers — that library only appears in this repo when the library *under test* literally is Testcontainers. `pulsar-client-all`'s POM dependency list confirms it's a true uber-artifact (bouncycastle, opentelemetry, jackson-annotations, caffeine all transitively bundled), so the gap isn't a missing Maven coordinate — it's that produce/consume/schema code paths are simply unreachable without a live broker on `pulsar://localhost:6650`.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

Research summary: checked the Maven Central POM for `pulsar-client-all:4.2.5` (no missing dependencies — it's self-contained), confirmed via Pulsar docs that the client needs a running broker at `pulsar://localhost:6650` for any meaningful produce/consume/schema/compression coverage, verified `apachepulsar/pulsar:4.2.5` exists on Docker Hub (exact version match, multi-arch), and cross-checked this repo's existing broker-client tests (`JnatsTest.java`, mosquitto) which all use a hand-rolled `docker run` in `@BeforeAll` rather than Testcontainers — no pulsar image is currently pinned in the allow-list.

